    "body": "So after doing some testing, it seems almost all fish prompts in omf have this behaviour. \r\n\r\nThis is likely because the simplest way to implement this functionality is to read out of `cmd_duration` in fish, which `fish` does not reset on blank command, unlike in zsh/bash where it has to be reset via a pre-execution hook and cannot be retained on blank command.\r\n\r\nI'm open to discussing what we think the correct behaviour should be, but given that we are consistent with the themes in omf that I tested, I'm going to consider this to not be a bug for now.",
